d #edb/ref 17592186069551 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068684 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068545 :question/id #uuid "e18e4cc8-8ecb-53e9-8b12-c9cb5b926aa7" :question/math-academy-id "e-3182"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89403c66-caac-5f6b-bacd-9f2a74525198" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069430} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069431} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497327}] :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"} :step/id #uuid "fb4b1e1c-564b-5857-b040-cc788b2e5510" :step/math-academy-id 10881} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497477 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497490 :tutorial/content "The problem of finding the length of a circle or a part of a circle often appears in real life. \n\nFor example, consider the pie in the shape of a circle divided into six equal slices, as shown in the figure below.\n\n![](images/48/48b416b9dffbf6e3e746e3fa8f90ec8043f937fe612e36e1219b5e9e8c368f22.png)\n\n How to find the total length of the border of one slice of pie?\n\nThe border of the slice of pie will consist of two parts:\n\n- the top and the bottom parts, which consist of two radii;\n\n- the right part (circular part), which consists of one-sixth of the circumference.\n\nFirst, let's find the length of the circular part. The formula for the circumference of a circle is ![](images/63/636374af24eb4d5c435de97b8e1ac460148deba4916b0954e3d1d2f7a364f9d7.svg) where ![](images/31/3122e2ea79ab0512edfce5c875a099de1a7067581b658d1b8fc9c105277aed36.svg) is the radius. Therefore, we have \n![](images/15/15bff81cb45d3df680e782e69534d2489388dfbcfd12b3cd579298d03f8bd452.svg)\n\nFinally, the length of the border is\n![](images/15/15037adbdea6b21d54991917b5dad6108c60257fd8f509300642343a101ebeeb.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "a14139c8-87eb-5e69-a268-c7cb088cf812" :tutorial/math-academy-id 15549 :tutorial/title "Calculating the Length of a Part of a Circle"} :step/id #uuid "cc9d4179-5034-59aa-b0e6-47636130b8db" :step/math-academy-id 643569 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069551}}] :activity/title "The Circumference of a Circle" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068987}]}
